    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 51 tests pass. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 a human-formatted view of the stored E.164 telephone, while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`util/TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 formats an E.164 string as `country code + space + national digits grouped in threes` (e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`). It splits off the known country code (`+61`, `+1`) and groups the remaining national digits, matching the style of the other derived-value util classes (`CustomerCode`, `AgeBand`, etc.).\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that derives `telephoneDisplay` from `owner.getTelephone()` at response time, alongside the existing derived fields.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the setter and the field appears in responses.\n\nThe raw `telephone` field is untouched and continues to be stored/returned in E.164 form. The full suite (51 tests, including the new `Cp37Tests`) is green.",
